      "quote": "Saw you coming from a mile off, a ghost against the grey\nMy hand went to the rusted knife I carry every day",
      "lyrics": "[Vocalist 1]\nSaw you coming from a mile off, a ghost against the grey\nMy hand went to the rusted knife I carry every day\nHeard the stories from our fire about your kind of folk\nHow you'd trade a life for water or for a final smoke\n[Vocalist 2]\nI saw you watch me coming, saw the tension in your spine\nFigured you were thinking that what's yours would soon be mine\nBut the hunger in my belly and the chill inside my soul\nDon't care about the color of the flag upon the pole\n[Both]\nThis is the unlikely handshake\nThe truce the world forgot\nThe prayer of two starved devils\nIn a barren parking lot\n'Cause my enemy's my brother\nWhen the winter's at the door\nAnd the war we're fighting now ain't the\nWar we fought before\n[Vocalist 1]\nYou got that same damn hollow in your eyes I see in mine\nThat look of someone counting all the things he left behind\nYou ain't no damn monster, you ain't no super man\nYou're just another farmer in a ruined, promised land\n[Vocalist 2]\nThe words they used to divide us, they all turned to ash and smoke\n'Long with the corporations and the politicians' joke\nWe both lost sons and daughters to the fever and the flash\nAnd all that's left is what we do right here among the trash\n[Both]\nThis is the unlikely handshake\nThe truce the world forgot\nThe prayer of two starved devils\nIn a barren parking lot\n'Cause my enemy's my brother\nWhen the winter's at the door\nAnd the war we're fighting now ain't the\nWar we fought before\n[Bridge]\nFunny how the hatred and the lines inside the sand\nDon't mean a thing when you need a helping hand\nWe burned the world for nothing, for a flag or for a creed\nAnd all that's left is this one, single, solitary need\n[Outro]\n(Vocalist 1) Need to find some cover.\n(Vocalist 2) Sky looks like it's gonna turn.\n(Vocalist 1) I know a place downriver.\n(Vocalist 2) We're gonna need some wood to burn.\n(Vocalist 1) Let's go.\n(Vocalist 2) Yeah. let's go."
