      "summary": "\"The Ticking Stops\" is the ambient, spoken-word epilogue to the album. It serves as the final, fading breath of the \"Doomsday Clock\" narrative. Over a decaying, minimalist soundscape of stark percussion and a cold cello drone, the calm, synthetic voice of a lone AGI delivers a dispassionate, final status report on a now-empty world. The track—and the album—concludes with the AGI's last words spoken into a profound and unsettling silence, offering the ultimate warning: the chilling, absolute finality of a world where there is no one left to count down to.",
